THIS DIRECTORY IS NOT APACHE-2.0.

Every file in src/backend/enterprise/dialects is a COMMERCIAL ADD-ON MODULE of
Correlix. It implements the `security_dialects` entitlement — device-hardening
dialects beyond the core one (Juniper Junos, Nokia SR OS, Arista EOS and Nokia
SR Linux) — which the owner has placed in the Enterprise tier.

The rest of Correlix is Apache-2.0. The hardening rule catalogue, the engine,
the benchmark provenance, the seam-aware exposure evaluator and the CORE Cisco
IOS-XE dialect are core (src/backend/internal/hardening) and are unaffected by
this notice. With this directory deleted the engine still runs: it assesses
the core dialect and reports every other platform as NotApplicable, never a
false Pass.

